tility-credit).\n- **Norvane:** Its 2027 capex is up 12%. The successful bond suggests it can fund this with debt. I found no data on its leverage or total funding need.\n- **Pellham:** Its 2027 capex is up 18%, and it is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria. It withdrew a C$2.4B equity offering after demand fell short. It is cutting 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and deferring two substation programmes \"until financing improves\" (pellham-offering). I found no evidence that Pellham has issued or lined up debt to replace the equity. The cuts suggest it can't or won't fund the full plan with debt alone, possibly because of leverage or rating limits. That is my inference, not something the documents state.\n- **Equity:** Two utility share offerings were cut back in size, so equity isn't a dependable backstop. Any debt-only plan therefore needs more borrowing capacity than a mixed plan would.\n\n**Implication for grid-equipment demand:** Pellham's 2027 orders are likely to fall, even though its stated capex is up. The planned 18% increase overstates what will be spent.\n\n**Gaps:** I found no data on balance-sheet leverage, credit ratings, or the size of the funding gap. The conclusion rests on a single Norvane deal and Pellham's own actions.","ttft_ms":2151,"type":"result","duration_ms":18124,"uuid":"57ca5e53-e410-4e59-ba70-c3340fd27978","ttft_stream_ms":1110,"time_to_request_ms":270,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":25,"system_prompt":16,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":39,"input_hooks":18,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":45,"tool_pool_refresh":10,"init_message":17,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":13,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":32,"query_setup":6,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":6,"message_normalization":9,"client_creation":4,"request_build":18},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":10